# USB device MTP: expose the SD card to a PC over MTP. Protocol engine lives in
# the SDK (bk_usb/bk_mtp/bk_usbd_mtp.c); the runtime start/stop control layer is
# solution/components/sdcard_mtp. Toggle at runtime via the `mtp start|stop` CLI.
#
# NOTE 1: USB_HOST is required even though MTP is a device-only gadget.
# usb_driver.c::bk_analog_layer_usb_sys_related_ops() (called from MTP bring-up to
# power the USB PHY/clock/OTG) and usb_dc_low_level_init() reference
# sys_ana_usb_phy_op / usb_clk_config / spitrig_toggle / usb_hc_riscv_ipi_enable,
# which are only defined in the host port file usb_hc_beken_musb.c (compiled under
# CONFIG_USB_HOST). The host stack stays dormant; only the device (MTP) path is
# ever brought up at runtime.
#
# NOTE 2: CONFIG_USB_RISCV_BRIDGE is deliberately OFF. Its device path is
# immature: usb_dc_riscv_device_prepare() now returns 0 (not the -1 stub the SDK
# comment claims), so the bridge takes over the USBD IRQ and the CP relays USB
# events to the AP via IPI -> usb_dc_riscv_poll_events() -> usbd_event_*_handler,
# which MemFaults on the first SUSPEND (bad pointer). With the bridge off,
# usb_dc_low_level_init() falls back to registering the mature M55-resident
# USBD_IRQHandler on INT_SRC_USB_HS -- the same path BK7259 uses for MSC U-disk.
CONFIG_USB=y
CONFIG_BK_USB_CHERRYUSB_V1_6=y
CONFIG_USB_DEVICE=y
CONFIG_USB_HOST=y
# CONFIG_USB_RISCV_BRIDGE is not set
CONFIG_USBD_MTP=y
CONFIG_USBD_MTP_PRODUCT_NAME="BekenMTP"
CONFIG_USBD_MTP_DEVICE_TYPE="1"
